{"id": "swebq0147", "pool": "swebq", "arm": "balanced", "tier": "balanced", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3259654580, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "452ae3d391103874253b2612ca88a459fb34e3c2c0d46a5f0ea415086d584f74", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.7972545623779297, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 6, "query": "who will be the red sox next coach?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/swebq0147.wav", "input_sha256": "14689c9b6682dcfb9aa153f224a904857589a3d0baebea8bd80f05104f6a5941", "input_samples": 34905, "input_s": 2.182, "n_real_chunks": 3, "score": 0.9021, "act": 0.9991, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "The Red Sox’s next manager/head coach is Chad Tracy — at least for now. Boston fired Alex Cora on April 25, 2026, and promoted Chad Tracy from Triple-A Worcester as interim manager. As of now, reports say Tracy getting the full-time job is “more likely than not,” but the Red Sox have not officially removed the interim tag yet. (mlb.com)", "expert_answer": "The **Red Sox’s next manager/head coach is Chad Tracy — at least for now**.\n\nBoston fired **Alex Cora** on **April 25, 2026**, and promoted **Chad Tracy** from Triple-A Worcester as **interim manager**. As of now, reports say Tracy getting the full-time job is **“more likely than not,”** but the Red Sox have **not officially removed the interim tag** yet. ([mlb.com](https://www.mlb.com/redsox/news/red-sox-dismiss-alex-cora-and-members-of-coaching-staff?utm_source=openai))", "transcript": "Who will be the Red Sox next coach?\n", "asr_s": 0.6, "expert_s": 6.94, "expert_input_samples": 34905, "expert_input_s": 2.182, "expert_input_sha256": "14689c9b6682dcfb9aa153f224a904857589a3d0baebea8bd80f05104f6a5941", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 0.0, "relay_synth_ms": 10103, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 10, "feed_lag_m